From 4f932e444875d7b0c2432151fa483016a7fbd3de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "mujiburrahimank@maxlinear.com"
 <mujiburrahimank@lvdocker7.lvsw.maxlinear.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:44:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-104137 Hostapd Crash due to EAPOL TX-status
 callback

Root Cause : The hostapd crash is triggered by a late EAPOL TX-status callback
after the STA has already been torn down. The failing path is the 802.1X
TX-status handling, which can still reach the WPA state machine after teardown.

sta->wpa_sm is cleared during station teardown, but the TX-status path was still
assuming the pointer was valid. That allowed a stale callback to dereference or
use a state machine that no longer belonged to the active authenticator.
The deeper guard in src/ap/wpa_auth.c was also too permissive for stale callers.

Resolution : The fix adds checks in both places below
- src/ap/ieee802_1x.c now returns early if sta->wpa_sm is NULL or no longer matches
the current hapd->wpa_auth.
- src/ap/wpa_auth.c now returns early if sm->wpa_auth != wpa_auth. That blocks late
TX-status events from reaching torn-down or detached WPA state and prevents the crash.

System Impact :  station connect/disconnect
---
 src/ap/ieee802_1x.c | 2 ++
 src/ap/wpa_auth.c   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c b/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c
index d0d0e54f2..0a8e04a72 100644
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c
@@ -2833,6 +2833,8 @@ int ieee802_1x_eapol_tx_status(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
 
 	if (len < (int) sizeof(*xhdr))
 		return 0;
+	if (!sta->wpa_sm)
+		return 0;
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "IEEE 802.1X: " MACSTR
 		   " TX status - version=%d type=%d length=%d - ack=%d",
 		   MAC2STR(sta->addr), xhdr->version, xhdr->type,
diff --git a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
index ce75bbe81..7b474dc70 100644
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
@@ -7140,7 +7140,7 @@ int wpa_auth_sta_set_vlan(struct wpa_state_machine *sm, int vlan_id)
 void wpa_auth_eapol_key_tx_status(struct wpa_authenticator *wpa_auth,
 				  struct wpa_state_machine *sm, int ack)
 {
-	if (!wpa_auth || !sm)
+	if (!wpa_auth || !sm || sm->wpa_auth != wpa_auth)
 		return;
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "WPA: EAPOL-Key TX status for STA " MACSTR
 		   " ack=%d", MAC2STR(wpa_auth_get_spa(sm)), ack);
-- 
